## Why This Is Asked
The scenario tests practical design of real-time telemetry pipelines across regions, emphasizing schema evolution, idempotency, backfill capability, and observability in a multi-tenant environment.

## Key Concepts
- Kinesis Data Streams, Lambda/Fargate, Glue Schema Registry, S3, Glue/Athena, DynamoDB, OpenTelemetry
- Schema evolution with backward/forward compatibility; idempotent sinks
- Backpressure handling and 24h backfill
- Per-region isolation and cost considerations

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: idempotent sink to DynamoDB
async function sink(event) {
  const key = `${event.deviceId}#${event.ts}`;
  const existing = await getItem(key);
  if (existing) return; // idempotent: skip duplicates
  await putItem({ ...event, id: key });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate schema evolution without breaking downstream consumers?
- What monitoring dashboards and SLAs would you implement to detect skew or lag across regions?

